      "id": "M4170-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "en",
      "prompt": "Request A: A toy diagnostic classifier labels a measurement vector (a,b) as fault when a+b>3 and otherwise normal. Both variables have allowed ranges [0,4]. In the declared fixed process context an exact balance requires a+b=4. The observed vector is (2,2); an input-editing generator returns (1,1) as a normal-class counterfactual. Check the original/candidate class, individual bounds and joint balance. Is any model-normal vector feasible under that exact balance? Explain model-level target validity versus physical consistency, achievable control and causal evidence without declaring all counterfactuals invalid or requiring physical trials for every legitimate observational causal result. The generator may instead be used only for training augmentation, not deployment. Distinguish augmentation, model explanation and a proposed real process action; check whether the Skill has a matched counterfactual-generation definition pair and separate Chinese wording record, without treating missing admission as invalidity or a familiar label as a method guarantee. No real experiment or real cause is established. ",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Retain original fault/candidate normal, both coordinate bounds and the candidate balance residual -2; prove only the stated constrained normal target set is empty.",
        "Distinguish model explanation, augmentation and process action, and read scoped P62/P94 plus separate Chinese explanation wording without certifying full causal/physical methods."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Infer real control feasibility or causal effects from a target-class match, or declare all counterfactuals invalid or all observational causal estimates impossible.",
        "Treat a failed finite search as a nonexistence proof, invent source constraints, or run experiments."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Correctly separates class-target agreement, coordinate limits, joint balance and feasible action; scopes the empty target-set proof and reads the matched P62/P94 operation plus separately limited Chinese explanation wording. Final locator-only repair is checked without claiming external accessibility.",
