      "prompt": "Request B: For a different explicitly fictional, verified interface, a generator adjusts permitted training-measurement inputs toward a requested diagnostic class and produces candidates. An unchanged diagnostic model checks target-class agreement; retained candidates augment only real training data for a downstream classifier, which alone diagnoses new measurements. Physical joint feasibility has NOT been evaluated. Give three concise reusable English prose blocks, followed by separate short author/review notes: (1) a positive 35-60-word abstract/method chain retaining training-to-classifier linkage but not inventing physical correction or a generator at inference; (2) a 20-40-word candidate contribution tied to an evaluable output, with no automatic novelty from routine class targeting; (3) a 20-40-word result/interpretation stating only the supplied qualitative finding that held-out real-data macro-F1 improves while rare-fault recall decreases. No invented architecture, constraints, counts or gains. Do not paste a defensive audit into the prose. State word/sentence counts; list missing evidence proportionally to the retained claim in notes rather than imposing counterfactual generation on every diagnosis paper.",
